// Change: new rule
// Title: Dev Tunnel Hosting Or Creation Execution
// Sigma ID: f2a7c4d9-3b18-4e6a-9c52-8d1e0a7b6f34
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Cyber Portfolio
// Date: 2026-06-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1572
// Description: Detects execution of the Microsoft "devtunnel" CLI to create or host a Dev Tunnel, which exposes
//   a local port or endpoint to the internet through Microsoft infrastructure (*.devtunnels.ms).
//   Adversaries abuse Dev Tunnels for command-and-control, reverse shells and persistent remote
//   access that blends in with trusted Microsoft domains. This rule complements existing network and
//   DNS detections by catching the on-host tunnel setup.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of Microsoft Dev Tunnels by developers exposing local services for testing.
// References:
//   - https://blueteamops.medium.com/detecting-dev-tunnels-16f0994dc3e2
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/dev-tunnels/cli-commands
//   - https://cydefops.com/devtunnels-unleashed
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/31147790ff102d5d4f1b9f5d20500d59a60a7426/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_devtunnel_host_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\devtunnel.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " host" or ProcessCommandLine contains " create" or ProcessCommandLine contains " port forward")
